  "content_text": "Kern On \n Tim Ahrens\n\n Kern on is a revolutionary kerning assistant that helps you cut down the time you spend kerning to just a few minutes. It takes care of kerning groups and your kerning. All it needs is a few kern pairs from you, then the plug-in ‘kerns on for you’.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 199€ \n → Get Kern On \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Show Stem Thickness \n Rafał Buchner\n\n View → Show Stem Thickness gives you a continuous measure of the stems, right at your finger tips.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Free \n → Get Plugin \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Speed Punk \n Yanone\n\n Speed Punk is a learning tool. It teaches you to better understand the nature of Bézier curves and their curvature, the technical basis of digital type design.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Free \n → Get Speed Punk \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Hellbox \n Jake Fleming\n\n Hellbox is a font proofing app for the Mac. It watches your Glyphs file and rebuilds real PDF proofs the moment you save: spacing strings, waterfalls, glyph sets, diacritics, and your own layouts. Double-click any glyph in a proof and it opens in an Edit view in Glyphs, so you go from spotting a problem to fixing it in one click.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 100$\n(students 50$) \n → Get Hellbox \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Remix Tools \n Just Another Foundry\n\n The Remix Tools are a set of plug-ins for Glyphs. They allow to harmonize glyph shapes, tune the width, automatically generate small caps, generate superior figures and much more.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 99€ \n → Get Remix Tools \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n LTTR/INK \n Martin Cetkovský & Filip Zajac\n\n Use stroke skeletons to speed up your work. LTTR/INK’s mighty nib force lets you draw with skeletons and control the stroke like never before. Forget outline editing, LTTR/INK generates perfectly plotted outlines, even directly to the exported font file.\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 50€+ \n → Get LTTR/INK",
